<h1>Date, DateTime and Time</h1>
<p><span class="cn">Aventus.Date</span> represents a calendar day, <span class="cn">Aventus.Time</span> a time of day, and <span class="cn">Aventus.DateTime</span> both. Methods such as <span class="cn">addDays()</span> and <span class="cn">with()</span> return a new value without changing the original.</p>

<h2 id="create-and-parse">Create and parse</h2>
<av-code language="typescript" filename="Example.lib.avt">
    <pre>
    const day = new Aventus.Date(2026, 11, 23);
    const parsedDay = Aventus.Date.parse("2026-11-23");
    const clock = Aventus.Time.parse("14:30:00");
    const appointment = Aventus.DateTime.parse("2026-11-23T14:30:00");
    const instant = Aventus.DateTime.parse("2026-11-23T13:30:00Z");
    &nbsp;
    console.log(Aventus.Date.today, Aventus.Time.now);
    console.log(Aventus.DateTime.now, Aventus.DateTime.utcNow);
    </pre>
</av-code>
<p><span class="cn">parse()</span> throws for invalid input; <span class="cn">tryParse()</span> returns <span class="cn">null</span>. Date uses <span class="cn">YYYY-MM-DD</span>, Time uses <span class="cn">HH:mm[:ss[.fraction]]</span>, and DateTime uses an ISO date and time with an optional <span class="cn">Z</span> or offset.</p>

<h2 id="arithmetic-and-comparison">Arithmetic and comparison</h2>
<av-code language="typescript" filename="Example.lib.avt">
    <pre>
    const nextWeek = day.addDays(7);
    const monthStart = day.startOfMonth();
    const later = clock.addMinutes(45); // Wraps at midnight.
    const deadline = appointment.addHours(2);
    &nbsp;
    console.log(day.isBefore(nextWeek));
    console.log(day.daysUntil(nextWeek)); // 7; diffDays() gives the absolute value.
    console.log(deadline.date, deadline.time);
    </pre>
</av-code>
<p>All three types offer <span class="cn">compareTo()</span>, <span class="cn">equals()</span>, <span class="cn">isBefore()</span> and <span class="cn">isAfter()</span>. Date and DateTime also provide year, quarter, month, week and day boundaries where applicable. Time differences compare times on the same day; they do not assume an overnight interval.</p>

<h2 id="time-zones">DateTime and time zones</h2>
<p>A DateTime without an offset represents a local date and time. An input ending in <span class="cn">Z</span> or containing an offset represents a specific instant and is converted to UTC. Specify a time zone such as <span class="cn">Europe/Zurich</span> before converting a local value to a timestamp or comparing it with a UTC value.</p>
<av-code language="typescript" filename="Example.lib.avt">
    <pre>
    const local = Aventus.DateTime.parse("2026-11-23T14:30:00");
    const utc = local.toUtc("Europe/Zurich");
    console.log(utc.toString()); // 2026-11-23T13:30:00Z
    console.log(local.toTimestamp("Europe/Zurich")); // Unix milliseconds.
    </pre>
</av-code>
<p><span class="cn">toUtc()</span> rejects local times that are ambiguous or do not exist because of a daylight saving change. Convert both values to UTC before comparing a local DateTime with a UTC DateTime.</p>

<h2 id="formatting">Formatting and configuration</h2>
<p><span class="cn">toString()</span> and <span class="cn">toJSON()</span> produce ISO values. Use <span class="cn">toLocaleString()</span> for display, or <span class="cn">toInputString()</span> for HTML time and date-time inputs. <span class="cn">configure()</span> shares formatting and calendar defaults across the three types; it does not change ISO parsing or JSON serialization.</p>
<av-code language="typescript" filename="Example.lib.avt">
    <pre>
    Aventus.Date.configure({ locale: "fr-CH", timeZone: "Europe/Zurich", firstDayOfWeek: 1 });
    console.log(day.toLocaleString());
    console.log(appointment.toInputString());
    console.log(clock.toInputString("minute"));
    </pre>
</av-code>
<p>Configuration also accepts <span class="cn">dateFormat</span>, <span class="cn">dateTimeFormat</span>, <span class="cn">timeFormat</span>, <span class="cn">monthNameFormat</span> and <span class="cn">dayNameFormat</span>. A supplied format object replaces the previous format object.</p>
